==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
The plan is to clear the Gregory and throw units into Corporal weyland's blindspot.
Stall the initial LeMurrs at base and build up a decent amount of money. Then rush the base and send out [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|A. Bahamut]] to kill the first General Gregory. Then send out some units to get into his blindspot. Literally anything under 300 standing range works. Also, any unit with decent dps and a short enough foreswing can be used to just brute force down the entire stage.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Due to the new threats appearing in this version of the stage, you can use anti-alien crowd-controllers to permanently freeze the [[Bun Bun Symbiote]], allowing your units to kill him quickly and deal with the [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]]. After you deal with the remaining peons, you should be able to easily kill them, as his long attck frequency prevents him from defending himelf from your crowd-control units.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
In this stage, [[Axoloty]] is introduced, posing a new threat to your units as Axoloty's waves are able to instantly kill anything in it's range. You can complete this stage by breaking his shield with a barrier breaker such as [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kitty of Liberty]] and then send high damage attackers such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to finish Axoloty off, as his extremely long attack frequency prevents him from continuously sending waves, allowing you to send your high damage dealers to kill him.

